      "snippet": "Squarespace Developer Platform: APIs, Apps, and Docs (https://developers.squarespace.com/mcp/overview)\n【turn61search0】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; If you're a developer building an experience for your users and connecting your own app or agent directly to the Squarespace MCP server, for example to add domain search to your product, your use is governed by our Developer Terms of Use. ... Domains  | Brainstorm business names, check domain availability and pricing, and get a link to buy a domain on Squarespace. ... The Commerce tools read and change a website, so they need you to sign in with your Squarespace account.\n\nThe Domains tools work for anyone, with no Squarespace account required.\n\nThe Commerce tools read and change a website, so they need you to sign in with your Squarespace account. They only appear in your client once you've signed in, and they act with your own permissions: an assistant can only see and change what you could see and change yourself in that website's Commerce panel. See Connect a Client.\n\n### Working with a website\n\nEvery signed-in tool works on one website at a time. If it isn't clear which site you mean, the assistant will ask, then keep using that site for the rest of the conversation until you ask to switch.\n\n### What the tools can and can't change\n\n  * Domains tools never buy anything. They return a checkout link. A domain is only registered when someone opens that link and completes checkout on squarespace.com.\n  * Commerce tools don't move money. They can create and update contacts and products, but they can't take payments, issue refunds, or fulfill orders. Orders are read-only.\n  * Changes are real. A product or contact the assistant creates or edits is saved to your live website. New products are hidden from shoppers until you (or the assistant, if you ask) publish them.\n\nMost MCP clients ask you to approve a tool before it makes a change. Keep that approval step turned on for tools that write to your website.\n\n## Supported cl"
