      "snippet": "Developer Tools APIs at Squarespace – Squarespace Help Center (https://support.squarespace.com/hc/en-us/articles/41325887099533-Developer-Tools-APIs-at-Squarespace)\n【turn61search1】 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; ## Use the Squarespace MCP server to connect AI assistants ... Developers can find the current list of tools and setup steps in our MCP developer documentation.\n  * Contacts API\n  * Discounts API\n  * Domains Search API\n  * Domains Management API\n  * Incoming Webhooks API\n  * Inventory API\n  * Orders API\n  * Products API\n  * Profiles API\n  * Reseller API\n  * Scripts API\n  * Transactions API \n  * UI Component Registrations API\n  * Webhook Subscriptions API\n\n## Use the Squarespace MCP server to connect AI assistants\n\nThe Squarespace MCP server connects AI assistants, like Claude and ChatGPT, to Squarespace tools using Model Context Protocol (MCP). Tools are organized by product area, like domains and commerce, and we add new tools over time. Developers can find the current list of tools and setup steps in our MCP developer documentation. If you use an AI assistant, you can also connect Squarespace to it and use Squarespace tools, like domain search and store management, in the middle of any conversation.\n\n## What terms apply when I use Squarespace developer tools?\n\nThe terms that apply depend on how you use our developer tools:\n\n  * If you’re a developer building with our APIs or MCP server to do things like add domain search to your product, create a product integration for your users who also use Squarespace, or otherwise taking part in a Squarespace developer program, our Developer Terms of Use cover your use case.\n  * If you’re using Squarespace via an AI assistant to do things like search for a domain or manage your use of Squarespace, our Terms of Service cover your use case."
