    {
      "url": "https://commerce-apis.squarespace.com/commerce-apis/authentication-and-permissions",
      "requested_url": "https://commerce-apis.squarespace.com/commerce-apis/authentication-and-permissions",
      "status": 200,
      "title": "Authentication and permissions — Squarespace Developers (https://commerce-apis.squarespace.com/commerce-apis/authentication-and-permissions)",
      "text": "Authentication and permissions — Squarespace Developers Getting started Overview Authentication and permissions Making requests Retrieve basic site information Using Commerce APIs Idempotency-Key header Rate limits Responses & error handling Upgrade Changelog Price Limits Glossary FAQ Inventory API Overview GET: Retrieve all inventory GET: Retrieve specific inventory POST: Adjust stock quantities Orders API Overview POST: Create an order POST: Fulfill an order GET: Retrieve all orders GET: Retrieve a specific order Products API Overview About product attributes Managing attributes POST: Create a product POST: Create a product variant POST: Upload a product image GET: Retrieve all Store Pages GET: Retrieve all products GET: Retrieve specific products GET: Product image upload status POST: Assign a product image to variant POST: Reorder a product image POST: Update a product POST: Update a product variant POST: Update a product image DEL: Delete a product DEL: Delete a product variant DEL: Delete a product image Profiles API Overview GET: Retrieve all profiles GET: Retrieve specific profiles Transactions API Overview GET: Retrieve all transactions GET: Retrieve specific transactions Webhook Subscriptions API Overview POST: Create a webhook subscription POST: Update a webhook subscription GET: Retrieve all webhook subscriptions GET: Retrieve a specific webhook subscription DEL: Delete a webhook subscription POST: Send test notification POST: Rotate a subscription secret Authentication and permissions To keep Squarespace merchant site data private and secure,\nevery request to Commerce APIs must be authenticated and have minimum permissions.\nHowever, authenticated requests automatically have access to public site data,\nsuch as site name, identifier, language, currency, time zone, and location. Read the permission levels for each Commerce API below.\nThen, depending on your development needs,\nauthenticate requests by using an API key or OAuth access token. Remember: Requests only have access to data for\nthe website that owns the API key or OAuth access token. API permission levels Forms API Read Only : View form submission data; for Zapier integration only Inventory API Read Only : View inventory stock levels Read and Write : Manage inventory stock levels Orders API Read Only : View order, fulfillment, and customer information (name, email, address, and more) Read and Write : View customer information (name, email, address, and more); manage order and fulfillment information Products API Read Only : View product information, including information for any images and variants; view Store Page information Read and Write : Manage product information, including information for any images and variants; view Store Page information Profiles API Read Only : View the name, address, email, marketing preferences, and other profile information of customers, subscribers, and other website users Transactions API Read Only : View transactional order, donation data, and customer information (email) Authenticating requests Depending on your development needs,\nyou can use a generated API key or start the OAuth process with Squarespace\nto become a registered OAuth client. A Squarespace merchant site can use both\nAPI keys and OAuth for data access, but Squarespace Extensions are required to use OAuth. Custom applications With Squarespace's Commerce Advanced plan,\nyou can develop a custom application for a Squarespace merchant site. Follow the steps below to generate an API key for a custom application. Log in to a Squarespace site. In the left nav, click Settings ; scroll down and click Advanced . Click Developer API Keys . Click the GENERATE KEY button. In the dialog, add a key name under \"KEY NAME\",\nand select one or more Commerce APIs under \"PERMISSIONS\" and permission level. Record the generated key in a safe and secure place. For security reasons, this is the only time the API key is visible.\nAPI keys will never expire as long as the merchant site remains active. Commercial development Squarespace Extensions allow customers on any plan\nto optimize and expand their site in a few clicks.\nIf you'd like to develop a new Extension,\nstart the OAuth client process by filling out this form .\nOnce you've obtained OAuth credentials, you can use our OAuth 2.0 Guide to learn how to authorize your application to integrate with Squarespace and use Squarespace APIs. Next steps Make requests to Commerce APIs Read the FAQ for answers to common questions Read our brand guidelines"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://developers.squarespace.com/mcp/overview",
      "requested_url": "https://developers.squarespace.com/mcp/overview",
      "status": 200,
      "title": "Squarespace Developer Platform: APIs, Apps, and Docs (https://developers.squarespace.com/mcp/overview)",
      "text": "Squarespace Developer Platform: APIs, Apps, and Docs Menu Overview of the Squarespace MCP Server The Squarespace MCP server connects AI assistants to Squarespace. It's built on the Model Context Protocol , an open standard for connecting AI applications to outside tools, so assistants like Gemini, Claude, and ChatGPT can look things up and make changes on Squarespace in the middle of a conversation. With it, someone can describe a new business and leave the chat with a domain ready to buy, or ask \"which orders still need shipping?\" about their own store and get a live answer. Connect a Client â Add Squarespace to Gemini, Claude, ChatGPT, or another MCP client. Notice: If you are a Squarespace user who is accessing the Squarespace MCP server through an AI assistant, for example to search for a domain or manage your own website, your use is governed by our Terms of Service . If you're a developer building an experience for your users and connecting your own app or agent directly to the Squarespace MCP server, for example to add domain search to your product, your use is governed by our Developer Terms of Use . What you can do The server's tools are organized into groups. Each group has its own page describing what its tools do, what to ask for, and what to watch out for. Group What it's for Sign-in Domains Brainstorm business names, check domain availability and pricing, and get a link to buy a domain on Squarespace. Not required Commerce Find, create, and update contacts and products, and look up orders, on one of your websites. Currently only available in Claude and ChatGPT. Required How it works The Squarespace MCP server is a remote server. There's nothing to install. Your MCP client connects directly to: Code https://mcp.squarespace.com/mcp You don't call the tools yourself. You ask the assistant for something in plain language, and it decides which tools to call and in what order. The tool descriptions the assistant needs are sent by the server when it connects, so they don't need to be copied into your prompts. Signing in The Domains tools work for anyone, with no Squarespace account required. The Commerce tools read and change a website, so they need you to sign in with your Squarespace account. They only appear in your client once you've signed in, and they act with your own permissions: an assistant can only see and change what you could see and change yourself in that website's Commerce panel. See Connect a Client . Working with a website Every signed-in tool works on one website at a time. If it isn't clear which site you mean, the assistant will ask, then keep using that site for the rest of the conversation until you ask to switch. What the tools can and can't change Domains tools never buy anything. They return a checkout link. A domain is only registered when someone opens that link and completes checkout on squarespace.com. Commerce tools don't move money. They can create and update contacts and products, but they can't take payments, issue refunds, or fulfill orders. Orders are read-only. Changes are real. A product or contact the assistant creates or edits is saved to your live website. New products are hidden from shoppers until you (or the assistant, if you ask) publish them. Most MCP clients ask you to approve a tool before it makes a change. Keep that approval step turned on for tools that write to your website. Supported clients Squarespace is built into Gemini as a connected app, and the Domains tools also work in Claude, ChatGPT, and any client that supports remote MCP servers. The Commerce tools are currently only available in Claude and ChatGPT. See Connect a Client for setup steps. Connect a Client On this page What you can do How it works Signing in Working with a website What the tools can and can't change Supported clients"
    },
